      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor in STEM Education",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Clinical Assistant Professor in STEM Education Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Clinical Assistant Professor in STEM Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The College of Education application process is conducted through electronic communication. Required documents to upload to this posting are: (1) a letter of application, (2) a curriculum vitae, (3) list of at least three professional references to include e-mail addresses and phone numbers, and (4) unofficial transcripts for all earned degrees (upload as one PDF document under tab for “other supporting documents”). Also note that official transcripts will be required for all finalists. For all Finalist: The online submission of at least three (3) letters of recommendation (on letterhead) will be required from the references listed on the application as provided by the candidate. Each reference listed will be prompted by an email notification regarding when to upload their letter of recommendation to our online system on behalf of the candidate. Review of completed applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Inquiries should be addressed to Brooke Whitworth, Ph.D., bwhit@sc.edu , Search Committee Chair. Positions are advertised for a minimum of forty-five (45) days on our job website. After forty-five (45) days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Posting Details Posting Summary Logo Posting Number FAC00147PO26 Advertised Title Clinical Assistant Professor in STEM Education Campus Columbia College/Division College of Education Department CED Teacher Education Advertised Salary Range Salary commensurate with qualifications. Location of Vacancy Part/Full Time Full Time Hours per Week 37.5 Position Category Full-time Equivalent (FTE) Basis 9 months Work County Richland Tenure Information Professional Track Job Search Category Faculty About USC About University of South Carolina From the Upstate to the Lowcountry, the University of South Carolina system is transforming the lives of South Carolinians through the impact of our eight institutions and 20 locations throughout the state. More than 50,000 students are enrolled at one of eight institutions, including the research campus in Columbia and comprehensive four-year universities in Aiken, Upstate and Beaufort. In addition, our Palmetto College campuses in Salkehatchie, Union, Lancaster and Sumter enable students to earn associate or bachelor’s degrees through a combination of in-person, online or blended learning. All of our system institutions place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Veterans' Preference Statement The University of South Carolina is committed to equal opportunity and proudly values the skills and experience military veterans bring to our workforce. Across South Carolina, we are making veterans a priority for employment and recognize their vital contributions to our state and our communities. Benefits for FTE Positions The University of South Carolina (USC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers state employees a valuable benefits package, including health and life insurance, generous paid leave and retirement programs. To learn more about USC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Position Description Advertised Job Summary The Department of Teacher Education at the University of South Carolina seeks applications for a 9-month professional track position in STEM Education at the rank of Clinical Assistant Professor anticipated to begin August 2027. Job Responsibilities: Responsibilities of the successful candidate include: (a) teaching graduate and undergraduate coursework in one or more of mathematics education, science education, and STEM education; (b) delivering K – 12 transdisciplinary STE M and/or project-based education content and pedagogy; and ( c) supporting the service needs of the Ed.D. in Educational Practice and Innovation with a concentration in STEM Education program, the Department of Teacher Education, and the College of Education. Required Education and Experience Candidates must have earned a Ph.D. or Ed.D. in Mathematics Education, Science Education, Curriculum and Instruction, STEM Education, or a related field. Candidates must also have: (a) excellent teaching skills; (b) the ability to mentor doctoral students; ( c) evidence of a continued record of professional development which may include scholarly productivity, and (d) experience with online teaching/learning platforms (e.g., Blackboard, Zoom); (e) three years of experience working with P–12 students and/or teacher education candidates in schools; (f) the ability to incorporate innovative pedagogies around school and community based learning, and (g) the ability to collaborate with a wide range of colleagues and students. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience teaching undergraduate and graduate students is also preferred. Posting Detail Information Desired Start Date 08/16/2027 Job Open Date 10/19/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant The College of Education application process is conducted through electronic communication. Required documents to upload to this posting are: (1) a letter of application, (2) a curriculum vitae, (3) list of at least three professional references to include e-mail addresses and phone numbers, and (4) unofficial transcripts for all earned degrees (upload as one PDF document under tab for “other supporting documents”). Also note that official transcripts will be required for all finalists. For all Finalist: The online submission of at least three (3) letters of recommendation (on letterhead) will be required from the references listed on the application as provided by the candidate. Each reference listed will be prompted by an email notification regarding when to upload their letter of recommendation to our online system on behalf of the candidate. Review of completed applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Inquiries should be addressed to Brooke Whitworth, Ph.D., bwhit@sc.edu , Search Committee Chair. Positions are advertised for a minimum of forty-five (45) days on our job website. After forty-five (45) days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/213374 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other protected category under applicable law. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Other Supporting Documents List of References and Contact Information Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 Writing Sample(s)/Sample Publications Teaching Portfolio To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/214750": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor - Intensive English Program",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Adjunct Instructor - Intensive English Program Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Adjunct Instructor - Intensive English Program Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Positions are advertised for a minimum of five (5) business days on our job website. After five (5) business days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. We are only accepting applications submitted by October 30, 2026. Posting Details Posting Summary Logo Posting Number TMP02322PO26 Job Code Title Instructor Advertised Title Adjunct Instructor - Intensive English Program Campus Columbia College/Division Division of Academic Affairs and Provost Department PROV Global Carolina Salary Commensurate with experience Location of Vacancy Part/Full Time Part Time Hours per Week 26 Work Schedule Each term consists of courses taught 5 days a week for an 8-week period. Individual teaching schedules vary per term depending on the assigned classes and may range from 10-26 hours per week. Job Search Category Temporary Faculty About USC About University of South Carolina From the Upstate to the Lowcountry, the University of South Carolina system is transforming the lives of South Carolinians through the impact of our eight institutions and 20 locations throughout the state. More than 50,000 students are enrolled at one of eight institutions, including the research campus in Columbia and comprehensive four-year universities in Aiken, Upstate and Beaufort. In addition, our Palmetto College campuses in Salkehatchie, Union, Lancaster and Sumter enable students to earn associate or bachelor’s degrees through a combination of in-person, online or blended learning. All of our system institutions place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Benefits for Temporary Positions The University of South Carolina (USC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers temporary employees expected to work at least 30 hours per week health and life insurance, flexible spending accounts and retirement programs. To learn more about USC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Position Description Advertised Job Summary Performs all aspects of instruction for USC’s intensive English program to students from diverse cultural, ethnic, and linguistic backgrounds. Reviews all program materials and prepares all lessons, assessments, and class assignments. Evaluates learning outcomes and recommends students for retention or progression to USC . Reports to Director of English Programs for Internationals. Qualifications Master’s degree in Teaching English as a Second Language/Linguistics/Applied Linguistics/ TEFL OR Master’s degree in a related field with TEFL / TESL certification. Experience in an intensive English program preferred. Job Duties Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 3 Desired Start Date 10/19/2026 Proposed End Date 12/18/2026 Job Open Date 09/18/2026 Job Close Date 10/30/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant Positions are advertised for a minimum of five (5) business days on our job website. After five (5) business days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. We are only accepting applications submitted by October 30, 2026. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/213334 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other protected category under applicable law. Position Attributes Position Attributes Employees in Safety-Sensitive or Security-Sensitive positions will be subject to pre-employment and post-employment drug testing in accordance with University policy HR 1.95 Drug and Alcohol Testing. Safety/Security Sensitive or Requires a CDL No Hazardous weather category Non-Essential Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
