      "title": "Research Specialist",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Research Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Research Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Posting Details Posting Summary Logo Posting Number TMP02207PO26 Job Code Title Research Specialist I Advertised Title Research Specialist Campus Columbia College/Division Arnold School of Public Health Department ASPH Communication Sciences and Disorders Salary Commensurate with experience Location of Vacancy Part/Full Time Part Time Hours per Week 20 Work Schedule Monday through Friday from 8:30 AM to 5:00 PM. Schedule must remain flexible to meet the needs of the lab. Travel may be required. Job Search Category Post-doctoral About USC About University of South Carolina From the Upstate to the Lowcountry, the University of South Carolina system is transforming the lives of South Carolinians through the impact of our eight institutions and 20 locations throughout the state. More than 50,000 students are enrolled at one of eight institutions, including the research campus in Columbia and comprehensive four-year universities in Aiken, Upstate and Beaufort. In addition, our Palmetto College campuses in Salkehatchie, Union, Lancaster and Sumter enable students to earn associate or bachelor’s degrees through a combination of in-person, online or blended learning. All of our system institutions place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Benefits for Temporary Positions The University of South Carolina (USC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers temporary employees expected to work at least 30 hours per week health and life insurance, flexible spending accounts and retirement programs. To learn more about USC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Position Description Advertised Job Summary The purpose of this position is to support all aspects of data collection and data management for a research study investigating early indicators of DLD and dyslexia in bilingual children. The job involves administering child assessments to participants in school settings, scoring and entering data, and conducting reviews of assessment administration to ensure accurate data collection practices. This position will also support team operations by contributing to recruitment, retention, and communication efforts with participating families and schools. Qualifications High school diploma. Preferred applicants will have prior experience working with school-age children, Spanish proficiency, and a Bachelor’s degree. Job Duties Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 10/26/2026 Proposed End Date 06/30/2027 Job Open Date 10/12/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/212306 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of 