of South Carolina From the Upstate to the Lowcountry, the University of South Carolina system is transforming the lives of South Carolinians through the impact of our eight institutions and 20 locations throughout the state. More than 50,000 students are enrolled at one of eight institutions, including the research campus in Columbia and comprehensive four-year universities in Aiken, Upstate and Beaufort. In addition, our Palmetto College campuses in Salkehatchie, Union, Lancaster and Sumter enable students to earn associate or bachelor’s degrees through a combination of in-person, online or blended learning. All of our system institutions place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Veterans' Preference Statement The University of South Carolina is committed to equal opportunity and proudly values the skills and experience military veterans bring to our workforce. Across South Carolina, we are making veterans a priority for employment and recognize their vital contributions to our state and our communities. Benefits for FTE Positions The University of South Carolina (USC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers state employees a valuable benefits package, including health and life insurance, generous paid leave and retirement programs. To learn more about USC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Position Description Advertised Job Summary RESPONSIBILITIES : Maintain an active career as a composer through performances, recordings, publications, etc.; teach courses in undergraduate and graduate music theory as well as composition; help direct concerts of contemporary music and student composer concerts; direct graduate and undergraduate research as needed. This position will work at the University of South Carolina Columbia campus in Columbia, SC. The search process will continue until the position is filled, but priority screening will begin on or shortly after October 30, 2026. Required Education and Experience QUALIFICATIONS : Doctorate in music composition (D.M.A. or Ph.D.; ABD also considered); proven record of achievement and promise of developing a national reputation as a composer; evidence of the potential for successful teaching of undergraduate- and graduate-level music theory and composition coursework (including applied study and supervision of student research). Preferred Qualifications The School of Music vision statement identifies our core values, each of which are predicated on our five themes as a School: the pursuit of Excellence ; devotion to Student Success ; the production of Music Leaders ; preparation of the Musician-Educator ; and the creation of Diversely Skilled Musicians . We also embrace the ethos of music for all by advancing the major endeavor, Music for the Common Good: Carolina’s Public Music Initiative. The school encourages applications from candidates who demonstrate interests and abilities that align with these values Posting Detail Information Desired Start Date 08/16/2027 Job Open Date 09/03/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Apply at uscjobs.sc.edu, Upload a letter of application, curriculum vitae, and the contact information for at least three current letters of recommendation. Please be sure that the application materials address the responsibilities, qualifications, and core values as described above. Scores, recordings, and any other materials will only be requested of a select group of applicants. The search process will continue until the position is filled, but priority screening will begin on or shortly after October 30, 2026. Positions are advertised for a minimum of forty-five (45) days on our job website. After forty-five (45) days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/212796 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other protected category under applicable law. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References and Contact Information Optional Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
