      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications require: 1) application letter; 2) curriculum vitae; 3) research statement; 4) teaching statement; and 5) contact information for three references. Positions are advertised for a minimum of forty-five (45) days on our job website. After forty-five (45) days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Posting Details Posting Summary Logo Posting Number FAC00113PO26 Advertised Title Assistant Professor Campus Columbia College/Division Arnold School of Public Health Department ASPH Arnold School of Public Health Advertised Salary Range Salary commensurate with qualifications. Location of Vacancy Part/Full Time Full Time Hours per Week 37.5 Position Category Full-time Equivalent (FTE) Basis 9 months Work County Richland Tenure Information Tenure-Track/Tenured Job Search Category Faculty About USC About University of South Carolina From the Upstate to the Lowcountry, the University of South Carolina system is transforming the lives of South Carolinians through the impact of our eight institutions and 20 locations throughout the state. More than 50,000 students are enrolled at one of eight institutions, including the research campus in Columbia and comprehensive four-year universities in Aiken, Upstate and Beaufort. In addition, our Palmetto College campuses in Salkehatchie, Union, Lancaster and Sumter enable students to earn associate or bachelor’s degrees through a combination of in-person, online or blended learning. All of our system institutions place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Veterans' Preference Statement The University of South Carolina is committed to equal opportunity and proudly values the skills and experience military veterans bring to our workforce. Across South Carolina, we are making veterans a priority for employment and recognize their vital contributions to our state and our communities. Benefits for FTE Positions The University of South Carolina (USC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers state employees a valuable benefits package, including health and life insurance, generous paid leave and retirement programs. To learn more about USC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Position Description Advertised Job Summary The Arnold School of Public Health ( ASPH ) at the University of South Carolina ( USC ) invites applications for a tenure-track position in a discipline of public at the rank of Assistant Professor. This search is focused on recruiting a faculty member with expertise and interest in conducting translational research across a variety of clinical settings. The successful candidate will have an appreciation of health disparities that are endemic to South Carolina and will be expected to: 1) serve as a resource for individuals planning to conduct translational research, 2) function as a collaborator on existing and future research projects, and 3) develop a vibrant independent research career at USC . This position presents an excellent opportunity to collaborate with academic colleagues from different colleges and schools within the University and clinical colleagues engaged in a wide variety of medical disciplines and allied health professions (e.g., nursing, physical therapy, nutrition). It also will entail working closely with the community we are here to serve in a manner consonant with the principles of community-based participatory research ( CBPR ). The successful applicant will be expected to maintain an active research program; teach courses in their field of expertise, with a special focus on translational research; mentor graduate students; and contribute to their department, the Arnold School of Public Health, and USC through professional service. Located in the capital city of Columbia SC, USC is a comprehensive Carnegie University of High Research Activity and Community Engagement. USC has six Health Science Units in addition to ASPH : 1) School of Medicine in Columbia 2) School of Medicine in Greenville, 3) College of Nursing, 4) College of Pharmacy, 5) College of Social Work and 6) the College of Arts and Sciences. ASPH was founded in 1975. Among public universities in the US, the ASPH ranks second in overall enrollment and fourth in NIH funding. ASPH consists of six departments and several research centers that address topics such as disease prevention, nutrition and physical activity, cancer, health services and policy, rural and minority health, aging, and health disparities. All departments within public health, the school, and the university provide a strong collaborative environment for cross-disciplinary team science across the public health research continuum. More information about ASPH and the six department within the school can be found at www.sph.sc.edu . Columbia, SC enjoys more than 300 days of sunshine annually and has ready access to pristine beaches, lakes, rivers, and mountains. The city hosts historical and cultural attractions, festivals, performing arts and sporting events, parks and outdoor recreation including Congaree National Park and 50,000-acre Lake Murray. Required Education and Experience A qualified candidate will have an earned doctoral degree in some discipline of public health by the beginning date of employment. Demonstrated evidence of high-quality scholarly research, and the potential to successfully compete for external research funding. Preferred Qualifications . Posting Detail Information Desired Start Date 08/16/2027 Job Open Date 09/14/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Applications require: 1) application letter; 2) curriculum vitae; 3) research statement; 4) teaching statement; and 5) contact information for three references. Positions are advertised for a minimum of forty-five (45) days on our job website. After forty-five (45) days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/213126 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other protected category under applicable law. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References and Contact Information Research Statement Optional Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/213035": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Positions are advertised for a minimum of forty-five (45) days on our job website. After forty-five (45) days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. The University of South Carolina offers a valuable benefits package including but not limited to: Health and Life Insurance Retirement Programs Paid Tuition Dependent Scholarships Annual Leave Sick Leave 13 Paid Holidays (including an extended December holiday) Paid Parental Leave Professional Development Opportunities Click here to learn more about why you should work at USC. Posting Details Posting Summary Logo Posting Number FAC00101PO26 Advertised Title Assistant Professor Campus School of Medicine Columbia College/Division School of Medicine Columbia Department SOMC Cell Biology and Anatomy Advertised Salary Range $104,250 - $109,250 Location of Vacancy Part/Full Time Full Time Hours per Week 37.5 Position Category Full-time Equivalent (FTE) Basis 12 months Work County Richland Tenure Information Tenure-Track/Tenured Job Search Category Faculty About USC About University of South Carolina From the Upstate to the Lowcountry, the University of South Carolina system is transforming the lives of South Carolinians through the impact of our eight institutions and 20 locations throughout the state. More than 50,000 students are enrolled at one of eight institutions, including the research campus in Columbia and comprehensive four-year universities in Aiken, Upstate and Beaufort. In addition, our Palmetto College campuses in Salkehatchie, Union, Lancaster and Sumter enable students to earn associate or bachelor’s degrees through a combination of in-person, online or blended learning. All of our system institutions place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Veterans' Preference Statement The University of South Carolina is committed to equal opportunity and proudly values the skills and experience military veterans bring to our workforce. Across South Carolina, we are making veterans a priority for employment and recognize their vital contributions to our state and our communities. Benefits for FTE Positions The University of South Carolina (USC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers state employees a valuable benefits package, including health and life insurance, generous paid leave and retirement programs. To learn more about USC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Position Description Advertised Job Summary The University of South Carolina Floyd School of Medicine is looking for an Assistant Professor, Tenure track to join the Cell, Biology and Anatomy department. Job Summary : The Department of Cell Biology and Anatomy at the University of South Carolina Floyd School of Medicine invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor. Our department has a dynamic, collaborative faculty with research expertise in cardiovascular development and disease. Information on individual faculty research interests is available at our website: Cell, Biology and Anatomy . Ideal candidates will have scientific interests that synergize with current department research activities while broadening our existing strengths and bringing new scientific approaches to the department. South Carolina is an NIH IDeA state which could provide applicants the opportunity to participate in multi-investigator/institutional grants at USC such as NIH Centers of Biomedical Research Excellence (COBREs), the Center for Clinical and Translational Research (an NIH CTR -D), and the SC IDeA Network of Biomedical Research Excellence (SC INBRE ) programs. In addition to our commitment to cutting edge research, the department contributes significantly to the educational mission of the School of Medicine by teaching in both the medical and graduate Biomedical Sciences programs. Skills/knowledge/abilities: Scientific writing experience evidenced by publications is required; Ability to give oral scientific presentations is expected; Participation in educating medical and graduate students Applicants are expected to have teaching interests, and potentially experience, that would allow integration into departmental educational responsibilities which include courses in human anatomy, histology, cell biology, biochemistry, and cardiovascular sciences. If interested submit your application to include: Cover letter indicating how the applicant’s research plan and teaching interests fit within and complement the department Curriculum vitae Research plans – a two-page description of future research plans Teaching statement – up to two-page teaching statement which includes mentoring philosophy Complete contact information for at least three references through the University of South Carolina online jobs portal (insert link). Required Education and Experience Applicants must hold a Ph.D., M.D., or M.D./Ph.D. with postdoctoral experience. The successful candidate will be expected to establish and maintain an independent, externally funded research program. Preferred Qualifications The preferred candidate will have appropriate postdoctoral experience and clear potential to establish an extramurally funded research program in cardiovascular development or disease related areas. Posting Detail Information Desired Start Date 01/01/2027 Job Open Date 09/10/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Positions are advertised for a minimum of forty-five (45) days on our job website. After forty-five (45) days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. The University of South Carolina offers a valuable benefits package including but not limited to: Health and Life Insurance Retirement Programs Paid Tuition Dependent Scholarships Annual Leave Sick Leave 13 Paid Holidays (including an extended December holiday) Paid Parental Leave Professional Development Opportunities Click here to learn more about why you should work at USC . Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/212837 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other protected category under applicable law. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References and Contact Information Teaching Statement Research Statement Optional Documents Other Supporting Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/212991": {
      "title": "Instructor / Senior Instructor in Cardiovascular Sciences",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Instructor / Senior Instructor in Cardiovascular Sciences Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Instructor / Senior Instructor in Cardiovascular Sciences Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. All applicants must apply online through USCJobs at https://uscjobs.sc.edu . Submit your application using the following link: https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/212949 . A complete application includes: (1) a cover letter; (2) a clinical practice teaching statement describing the candidate's cardiovascular professional experience, teaching and mentoring interests, and relevant administrative, curriculum-development, and scholarly experience; (3) a curriculum vitae; and (4) the names and email addresses of three professional references. Positions are advertised for a minimum of forty-five (45) days on our job website. After forty-five (45) days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. The University of South Carolina offers a valuable benefits package including but not limited to: Health and Life Insurance Retirement Programs Paid Tuition Dependent Scholarships Annual Leave Sick Leave 13 Paid Holidays (including an extended December holiday) Paid Parental Leave Professional Development Opportunities Click here to learn more about why you should work at USC. Posting Details Posting Summary Logo Posting Number FAC00107PO26 Advertised Title Instructor / Senior Instructor in Cardiovascular Sciences Campus Columbia College/Division College of Arts and Sciences Department CAS Biological Sciences Advertised Salary Range We offer a competitive salary and benefits package. Location of Vacancy Part/Full Time Full Time Hours per Week 40 Position Category Full-time Equivalent (FTE) Basis 12 months Work County Richland Tenure Information Professional Track Job Search Category Faculty About USC About University of South Carolina From the Upstate to the Lowcountry, the University of South Carolina system is transforming the lives of South Carolinians through the impact of our eight institutions and 20 locations throughout the state. More than 50,000 students are enrolled at one of eight institutions, including the research campus in Columbia and comprehensive four-year universities in Aiken, Upstate and Beaufort. In addition, our Palmetto College campuses in Salkehatchie, Union, Lancaster and Sumter enable students to earn associate or bachelor’s degrees through a combination of in-person, online or blended learning. All of our system institutions place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Veterans' Preference Statement The University of South Carolina is committed to equal opportunity and proudly values the skills and experience military veterans bring to our workforce. Across South Carolina, we are making veterans a priority for employment and recognize their vital contributions to our state and our communities. Benefits for FTE Positions The University of South Carolina (USC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers state employees a valuable benefits package, including health and life insurance, generous paid leave and retirement programs. To learn more about USC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Position Description Advertised Job Summary The Cardiovascular Technology ( CVT ) Program and the Department of Biological Sciences in the McCausland College of Arts and Sciences at the University of South Carolina invites applications for a full-time, professional track faculty position at the rank of Instructor or Senior Instructor , to begin August 16, 2027 . The position is a twelve-month appointment with 50% teaching and 50% administrative service. This is an annual appointment that may be renewed contingent upon the dean’s approval, satisfactory performance, department needs and the availability of funding. We seek an experienced cardiovascular professional and educator who can bridge a rigorous undergraduate cardiovascular science education with contemporary clinical practice to help strengthen and expand our CVT major. Teaching: The successful candidate is expected to teach and mentor undergraduate students preparing for careers in CVT and related health sciences. Primary responsibilities to include instruction of: · Advanced cardiovascular anatomy and physiology, including clinically relevant pathophysiology, hemodynamics, and foundations of diagnostic and interventional cardiovascular procedures. · A professional development course that introduces students to the roles and responsibilities of a cardiovascular technologist, interprofessional communication, patient-centered care, and workplace professionalism. · Additional instruction and mentoring support as needed in Cardiovascular Health Sciences and in the Department of Biological Sciences. Administration and program development: The successful candidate is expected to help strengthen and expand the CVT program’s network of clinical training partners by : · Developing additional partnerships with CAAHEP -accredited cardiovascular technology training programs . · Managing and strengthening affiliation agreements and relationships with hospitals, clinical educators, and program directors of certificate training programs. · Contributing to the development, review, and improvement of Cardiovascular Sciences and related curriculum. · Complementing our professional student advisors in helping students transition from undergraduate study into affiliated clinical training programs and cardiovascular careers. USC’s Cardiovascular Technology major combines a rigorous science-based undergraduate curriculum with intensive clinical training through accredited partner programs, preparing students for professional cardiovascular technology practice, leadership, and further study. Current opportunities exist for training in adult echocardiography , vascular sonography , combined echo/vascular, invasive cardiovascular technology , and electrophysiology . Visit https://www.sc.edu/study/colleges_schools/artsandsciences/academics/degrees/cdvt/ for more information. Required Education and Experience Candidates must have: (1) A master’s degree in cardiovascular sciences, health sciences, kinesiology, physiology, exercise science, or a closely related field by employment start date. (2) At least 2 years of professional experience in cardiovascular technology, diagnostics/intervention, or a closely related field with (3) current or previous professional certification/registration such as RCIS , RDCS , RVT , RCES , RCS , RVS , or equivalent nationally recognized cardiovascular credential. (4) Sufficient instructional experience to teach advanced cardiovascular anatomy and physiology and prepare students for cardiovascular clinical practice. (5) Strong communication, organizational, mentoring, and collaborative skills. Appointment as Senior Instructor requires the equivalent of five years of full-time teaching experience in higher education. Candidates with evidence of research scholarship, quality-improvement and workforce development, professional leadership, or other contributions to cardiovascular education and clinical practice are encouraged to apply. Preferred Qualifications Posting Detail Information Desired Start Date 08/16/2027 Job Open Date 09/09/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant All applicants must apply online through USCJobs at https://uscjobs.sc.edu . Submit your application using the following link: https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/212949 . A complete application includes: (1) a cover letter; (2) a clinical practice teaching statement describing the candidate’s cardiovascular professional experience, teaching and mentoring interests, and relevant administrative, curriculum-development, and scholarly experience; (3) a curriculum vitae; and (4) the names and email addresses of three professional references. Positions are advertised for a minimum of forty-five (45) days on our job website. After forty-five (45) days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. The University of South Carolina offers a valuable benefits package including but not limited to: Health and Life Insurance Retirement Programs Paid Tuition Dependent Scholarships Annual Leave Sick Leave 13 Paid Holidays (including an extended December holiday) Paid Parental Leave Professional Development Opportunities Click here to learn more about why you should work at USC . Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/212949 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other protected category under applicable law. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a minimum Master’s Degree in Cardiovascular Sciences, Health Sciences, Kinesiology, Physiology, Exercise Science, or a closely related field by employment start date? Yes No * Do you have at least 2 years of professional experience in cardiovascular technology, diagnostic/intervention, or a closely related field? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References and Contact Information Teaching Statement Optional Documents Other Supporting Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
