    "https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/212902": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "University of South Carolina | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Initial review of applicants will commence October 12, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. The appointment start date will be August 16, 2027. The required application documents for consideration include: 1) a letter of intent describing how the candidate’s professional/academic experiences and research profile match the position 2) a current curriculum vitae/resume. 3) a list of three professional references and contact information Final-round candidates must submit three recommendation letters on official letterhead with physical signatures (no typed names) and an official transcript from an accredited degree-granting institution. Letters should be sent directly to the search committee chair via the previously mentioned email. Degrees earned outside the U.S. must be evaluated by a USC-approved credential evaluator . Questions may be directed to the search committee chairperson, Dr. Mark Nagel (email: NAGEL@sc.edu ). Positions are advertised for a minimum of forty-five (45) days on our job website. After forty-five (45) days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Posting Details Posting Summary Logo Posting Number FAC00099PO26 Advertised Title Assistant Professor Campus Columbia College/Division College of Hospitality, Retail and Sport Management Department HRSM Sport and Entertainment Management Advertised Salary Range Salary is commensurate with qualifications and experience Location of Vacancy Columbia, SC Part/Full Time Full Time Hours per Week 37.5 Position Category Full-time Equivalent (FTE) Basis 9 months Work County Richland Tenure Information Tenure-Track/Tenured Job Search Category Faculty About USC About University of South Carolina From the Upstate to the Lowcountry, the University of South Carolina system is transforming the lives of South Carolinians through the impact of our eight institutions and 20 locations throughout the state. More than 50,000 students are enrolled at one of eight institutions, including the research campus in Columbia and comprehensive four-year universities in Aiken, Upstate and Beaufort. In addition, our Palmetto College campuses in Salkehatchie, Union, Lancaster and Sumter enable students to earn associate or bachelor’s degrees through a combination of in-person, online or blended learning. All of our system institutions place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Veterans' Preference Statement The University of South Carolina is committed to equal opportunity and proudly values the skills and experience military veterans bring to our workforce. Across South Carolina, we are making veterans a priority for employment and recognize their vital contributions to our state and our communities. Benefits for FTE Positions The University of South Carolina (USC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers state employees a valuable benefits package, including health and life insurance, generous paid leave and retirement programs. To learn more about USC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Position Description Advertised Job Summary The David and Nicole Tepper Department of Sport and Entertainment Management at the University of South Carolina invites applications for a full-time, tenure track Assistant Professor of College Sport Business in one of the nation’s premier programs. The successful candidate will develop a nationally recognized program of research focused on the forces shaping the evolving landscape of U.S. college sport. Areas of interest may include, but are not limited to, the business and economic models of college athletics; revenue generation and distribution; athlete compensation and revenue sharing; conference and institutional strategy; governance and organizational structure; the relationship between athletics and the mission and business model of higher education; legal and policy developments affecting college sport; and the long-term financial and organizational sustainability of intercollegiate athletics. The successful candidate will also have opportunities to contribute to the College Sport Research Institute ( CSRI ) and its mission of advancing interdisciplinary research, fostering collaboration among college-sport scholars, and disseminating research to academics, practitioners, policymakers, and the broader public. As a 9-month faculty member on the Columbia, South Carolina, campus, the successful candidate will develop and sustain a program of excellence in research, teach courses in Sport and Entertainment Management, pursue external funding opportunities related to research agenda, provide mentoring and guidance to students in the major, collaborate with other departmental faculty in the general mission of the unit; and serve on Department, College, or University committees as needed. The successful candidate will join a collaborative faculty committed to shaping the future of sport, entertainment, and venue management through excellence in teaching, research, service to the discipline, and industry engagement. The University of South Carolina’s David and Nicole Tepper Department of Sport and Entertainment Management is a leader in the field, offering B.S., MSEM , and Ph.D. programs that prepare students for successful careers in sport, entertainment, and venue management. As the largest and first program of its kind, the department recognized for our innovative approach to education, cutting-edge research, and industry-leading faculty. The innovative curriculum and strong industry partnerships create unparalleled opportunities for both faculty and students. If you are passionate about shaping the future generation of industry leaders in Sport and Entertainment Management and thrive in a collaborative, forward-thinking environment, we invite you to explore this opportunity. Required Education and Experience Earned doctorate in Sport Management, Entertainment Management, or related-field discipline by the start date of the employment (ABDs considered). Primary teaching and research interests in Sport and Entertainment in one or more of the following high-demand areas: the business of U.S. college sport, athlete branding and NIL , college sport governance. Other areas of interest include finance, analytics, marketing and sponsorship, sales, event operations, law and governance, leadership, and venue management. An active research agenda with a demonstrated ability to generate impactful, peer-reviewed research in premier outlets. Strong evidence of (or potential to attract) external funding and a demonstrated ability to deliver high quality classroom instruction. Preferred Qualifications Posting Detail Information Desired Start Date 08/16/2027 Job Open Date 09/03/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Initial review of applicants will commence October 12, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. The appointment start date will be August 16, 2027. The required application documents for consideration include: 1) a letter of intent describing how the candidate’s professional/academic experiences and research profile match the position 2) a current curriculum vitae/resume. 3) a list of three professional references and contact information Final-round candidates must submit three recommendation letters on official letterhead with physical signatures (no typed names) and an official transcript from an accredited degree-granting institution. Letters should be sent directly to the search committee chair via the previously mentioned email. Degrees earned outside the U.S. must be evaluated by a USC -approved credential evaluator . Questions may be directed to the search committee chairperson, Dr. Mark Nagel (email: NAGEL@sc.edu ). Positions are advertised for a minimum of forty-five (45) days on our job website. After forty-five (45) days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/212802 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other protected category under applicable law. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References and Contact Information Optional Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
