 Carolina, the state’s capital, the Moore School offers the advantages of a vibrant, affordable, and highly livable city. Columbia features a thriving arts and cultural scene, abundant outdoor recreation, and convenient access to both the Atlantic coast and the Blue Ridge Mountains, making it an exceptional place to live and work. The Finance Department at the Darla Moore School of Business, University of South Carolina, seeks a high-potential faculty member committed to excellence in teaching and research. The successful candidate will have expertise in finance, including areas such as risk management and insurance and real estate. Required Education and Experience Applicants must have completed a PhD by the employment start date (August 16, 2027). Candidates who are ABD at the time of application are welcome to apply. Successful applicants must demonstrate the potential for excellence in teaching at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. Preferred Qualifications Posting Detail Information Desired Start Date 08/16/2027 Job Open Date 07/02/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Applications should include a curriculum vitae, three samples of research, evidence of teaching excellence, and three letters of recommendation. Letters of recommendation should be submitted directly by the references to finance.search@moore.sc.edu. Positions are advertised for a minimum of forty-five (45) days on our job website. After forty-five (45) days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. The University of South Carolina offers a valuable benefits package including but not limit