candidates from a full spectrum of methodological orientations. This position is part of a cluster of targeted hires supported by a broader presidential hiring initiative, which will offer a cohort of incoming scholars sharing focus on these broad themes, enhancing sociology’s contributions to this initiative. Successful candidates will be expected to maintain an active program of research, teach, contribute to departmental service, and mentor graduate students in our Ph.D. program. Required Education and Experience Applicants must have a PhD degree in sociology or a closely related field by the start date of employment. Preferred Qualifications Posting Detail Information Desired Start Date 08/16/2026 Job Open Date 09/08/2025 Job Close Date 03/12/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Applications must include: (1) a cover letter that describes their research and teaching interests (2-3 pages), (2) a curriculum vitae, (3) a writing sample exemplar of their research germane to the position, and (4) the names and email addresses of 3 references, who will not be contacted until after the initial screening process. We will begin reviewing applications on Oct 10, 2025. Inquiries about this position may be directed to Recruitment Chair jimi adams – jimi.adams@sc.edu. Positions are advertised for a minimum of five (5) business days on our job website. After five (5) business days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/194374 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in educational or employment opportuniti