uate courses including, but not limited to, college algebra, finite and discrete mathematics, precalculus, applied calculus, calculus, differential equations, and linear algebra. Required Education and Experience Requires a master’s degree in mathematics or mathematics education. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated record of excellence in teaching. Experience in teaching one or more of the following: college algebra, finite and discrete mathematics, precalculus, applied calculus, calculus, differential equations, and linear algebra. Posting Detail Information Desired Start Date 08/16/2026 Job Open Date 10/15/2025 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant All applicants must apply online at USCJobs at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Applicants may also apply via MathJobs at https://www.mathjobs.org, but an application will be considered complete only after submission through USCJobs. Applications must include: (1) a cover letter, (2) a statement of teaching philosophy, (3) teaching evaluations, (4) a current CV, and (5) at least three signed letters of recommendation specifically addressing the teaching of the applicant. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Inquiries about the position may be directed to Dr. Matthew Boylan at boylan@math.sc.edu. Positions are advertised for a minimum of five (5) business days on our job website. After five (5) business days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This position is open until filled. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/196136 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in educational or employme