      "description": "University of South Carolina | Post Doctoral Fellow Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search USC Market Titles Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Employee Login to View Position Description Post Doctoral Fellow Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Positions are advertised for a minimum of five (5) business days on our job website. After five (5) business days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. We are only accepting applications submitted by December 12, 2026. Posting Details To navigate through this form, please use the “Prev” and “Save & Continue” buttons at the top of the page. Do not use your browser’s “Back” button as it will not save your progress and data will be lost. Posting Summary Logo Posting Number RTF00251PO26 USC Market Title Post Doctoral Fellow Link to USC Market Title https://uscjobs.sc.edu/titles/156387 Business Title (Internal Title) Post Doctoral Fellow Campus Columbia Work County Richland College/Division College of Arts and Sciences Department CAS Psychology Anticipated Hiring Range $56,500 Location of Vacancy Part/Full Time Full Time Hours per Week 37.5 Work Schedule Standard schedule is Monday – Friday from 8:30 am to 5:00 pm with one hour for lunch. Must be willing to work a flexible schedule to meet the needs of the department. Type of Staff Position Staff Research Grant (SRGP) Basis 12 months Job Search Category Post-doctoral About USC About University of South Carolina From the Upstate to the Lowcountry, the University of South Carolina system is transforming the lives of South Carolinians through the impact of our eight institutions and 20 locations throughout the state. More than 50,000 students are enrolled at one of eight institutions, including the research campus in Columbia and comprehensive four-year universities in Aiken, Upstate and Beaufort. In addition, our Palmetto College campuses in Salkehatchie, Union, Lancaster and Sumter enable students to earn associate or bachelor’s degrees through a combination of in-person, online or blended learning. All of our system institutions place strong emphasis on service — helping to build healthier, more educated communities in South Carolina and beyond. Benefits for Research Grant or Time-Limited Positions Are Indicated Below The University of South Carolina (UofSC), through the State of SC and Public Employee Benefit Authority (PEBA), offers employees a valuable benefits package, including health and life insurance, generous paid leave and retirement programs. To learn more about UofSC benefits, access the \"Working at USC\" section on the Applicant Portal at https://uscjobs.sc.edu. Research Grant or Time-limited positions may be eligible for all, some, or no benefits, based on the grant or project funding. South Carolina Retirement Yes State Insurance Programs Yes Annual Leave Yes Sick Leave Yes Position Description Advertised Job Summary The Postdoctoral Fellow will conduct advanced research within the Feilong Lab using behavioral and neuroimaging methods. Primary responsibilities include data acquisition, data analysis, writing manuscripts, research presentations, and mentoring junior members of the lab. Job Related Minimum Required Education and Experience Requires a Doctoral (Ph.D.) degree in area of research specialty by the start date of employment. Required Certification, Licensure/Other Credentials Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. in Cognitive Neuroscience, Psychology, Cognitive Science, or a related field by the appointment start date. Experience with MRI data acquisition and analysis. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities Knowledge of cognitive neuroscience, behavioral research, and fMRI methods; skill in quantitative data analysis and scientific programming (e.g., Python or MATLAB ). Ability to design and conduct research, interpret findings, and communicate results clearly. Ability to work independently, collaborate with colleagues, and mentor junior researchers. Job Duties Job Duty Design and conduct independent and collaborative studies of the neural organization of affect and individual differences. Develop research questions and experimental paradigms, acquire behavioral and fMRI data using naturalistic stimuli, and document study procedures. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 35 Job Duty Preprocess and analyze behavioral, fMRI, and other multimodal data. Apply statistical and computational methods to address research questions, develop or adapt analysis pipelines, and assess data quality and reproducibility. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 25 Job Duty The Postdoctoral Fellow will write, revise, and submit manuscripts for peer-reviewed journals and present research findings at lab meetings, seminars, and scientific conferences. These activities will disseminate the Feilong Lab’s research on the neural organization of affect, contribute to the scientific literature, and promote collaboration and visibility for the lab’s work. The fellow will prepare clear written reports of study methods and results, respond to coauthor and reviewer feedback, and develop professional presentations tailored to academic and scientific audiences. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 15 Job Duty Mentor graduate and undergraduate students and other junior lab members in study design, data collection, analysis, and scientific writing. Provide scientific guidance and training within collaborative projects. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 10 Job Duty Contribute to grant proposals and progress reports by preparing methods, preliminary analyses, and other research documentation. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 10 Job Duty Maintains current knowledge of relevant research developments and methodological advances; participate in professional development opportunities; and contribute to laboratory and departmental activities that support the research program. Essential Function Yes Percentage of Time 5 Position Attributes Hazardous weather category Non-Essential Employees in Safety-Sensitive or Security-Sensitive positions will be subject to pre-employment and post-employment drug testing in accordance with University policy HR 1.95 Drug and Alcohol Testing. No Posting Detail Information Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 05/16/2027 Position End Date 05/15/2028 Job Open Date 10/28/2026 Job Close Date 12/12/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicant Positions are advertised for a minimum of five (5) business days on our job website. After five (5) business days, positions can be closed at the discretion of the department at any time. This employment site is updated on a regular basis. The length of the recruitment and screening process may vary from position to position, depending upon a variety of factors. Should review of your qualifications result in a decision to pursue your candidacy, you will be contacted by phone or email. We are only accepting applications submitted by December 12, 2026. Quicklink for Posting https://uscjobs.sc.edu/postings/215164 EEO Statement The University of South Carolina does not discriminate in employment opportunities or decisions for qualified persons on the basis of age, ancestry, citizenship status, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, veteran status, or any other protected category under applicable law. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you or will you have at least a Doctoral (Ph.D.) degree in area of research specialty by the start date of employment? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume List of References and Contact Information Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 Other Supporting Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
